  "slug": "simulations-structural-6310",
  "summary": "New work tests AlphaFold outputs against bilayer geometry and amyloid polymorphism, while a GPU frustratometer makes proteome-scale energetic analysis feasible.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is evaluating predicted or designed structures with physical criteria beyond a single static fold. AlphaFold-Multimer transmembrane complexes in the AFDB (~189k) are assessed for bilayer compatibility, with most showing plausible geometry. AlphaFold3 pseudo-ensembles are tested for recovering parallel versus antiparallel beta-sheet organization and polymorphism in short amyloidogenic peptides. The PyTorch Frustratometer reimplements local energetic frustration analysis with 70-13,000x GPU speedups and near-identical results, enabling proteome-scale use. The Omega-loop study adds a sequence-level view, reporting Gly/Pro enrichment and interface-dependent conservation using ProteinMPNN design modelling. The items differ in method, but together they move evaluation toward geometry, flexibility and energetics at scale.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
